@using DriveUnion.Web.Models
@model FilesPageViewModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = Model.Selected?.Name ?? UiText.Files.Title;
}

@*
    One file, on a page of its own.

    The panel on «فایل‌ها» draws exactly this — it is the same partial — and that is the point. What
    the panel could not do is be somewhere: pressing a file scrolled a column into view off to one
    side, so watching a film meant remembering to press the name, then scroll, then find the tile.
    Three steps and a memory for the one thing this product is for.

    A page has an address, so it can be linked, bookmarked, opened in a tab and gone back from.
*@
<div class="stack" style="gap: 14px;">
    @*
        Back to where the reader came from, with their search and folder intact. Losing those on the
        way back is what makes a list of two hundred files unusable — you find one, look at it, and
        are returned to the top of everything.
    *@
    <a class="btn btn--sm" href="@Url.Action("Index", "Files", new { q = Model.Query, folder = Model.Folder, tag = Model.Tag })">
        @UiText.Files.BackToFiles
    </a>

    <div class="file-page">
        @await Html.PartialAsync("_FileDetail", Model)
    </div>
</div>
